      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Upon the arrival of shipments in India, the final delivery phase initiates immediately with a rigorous daylight verification protocol. Natural light is essential for accurately inspecting exterior packaging conditions and identifying any transit damage that might be concealed under artificial indoor lighting.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">The receiving team must meticulously cross-reference the physical inventory against the original inventory bilty, ensuring that every listed item is present, accounted for, and matches the documented serial numbers or model identifiers.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This step is critical for establishing a clear chain of custody and addressing any discrepancies with the logistics provider before the goods are moved further into the facility.</span></li></ul>

<p>Following successful inventory verification, the operational team proceeds to the technical assessment of all electrical and mechanical components. A functional smoke test is conducted for each unit to verify power connectivity, operational stability, and the absence of immediate hardware faults.</p>
<p>For mechanical items, basic movement checks and safety feature validations are performed to ensure they meet the required operational standards. Any items failing these initial tests are immediately segregated for diagnostic review, preventing the integration of defective equipment into the active workflow and minimizing potential downtime.</p>

<p>Simultaneously, the placement of clean furniture requires precise coordination to protect both the items and the site infrastructure. Furniture pieces, having been cleared of all transit dust and protective films, are positioned according to the pre-approved layout plan.</p>
<p>This stage emphasizes gentle handling to avoid scratches or structural damage, ensuring that the aesthetic and functional integrity of the furnishings is preserved upon their first appearance in the operational space.</p>

<ul>
    <li>Conduct a thorough daylight inspection to verify packaging integrity and confirm exact match with the original bilty list.</li>
    <li>Execute functional tests on all electrical devices to check power, connectivity, and basic operational parameters.</li>
    <li>Perform mechanical checks on equipment to ensure moving parts function correctly and safety mechanisms are engaged.</li>
    <li>Position clean furniture according to the designated layout, ensuring no damage occurs during the final placement.</li>
    <li>Initiate swift removal of all packing debris, including cardboard, foam, and plastic wrapping, to maintain site hygiene.</li>
    <li>Dispose of waste materials in designated recycling or general waste bins to comply with local environmental regulations.</li>
    <li>Document the completion of all steps in the delivery log, noting any anomalies or specific conditions of delivered items.</li>
</ul>
<p>This comprehensive protocol ensures that the transition from transit to operational readiness is seamless, efficient, and free from logistical bottlenecks, thereby safeguarding the value of the delivered assets.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



